      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg per day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nThe order also needs to come from a licensed prescriber. A prescriber should enter it or confirm it directly.\n\n- **If 1000 mg was a typo**, tell me the intended dose. The usual adult range is 25\u2013200 mg once daily by mouth. I can enter it once a prescriber has confirmed it.\n- **If the dose is intentional**, for example as part of an unusual protocol, the prescriber and a pharmacist should verify it first. I can enter it with a note recording that verification."
      }
